This directory is GENERATED, but must exist in a fresh checkout.

`pubspec.yaml` declares `assets/schema/` as an asset directory, and Flutter
fails the build when a declared directory is missing. The JSON contract inside
it is copied from the repo-root `schema/` (the single source of truth, which IS
tracked) and is gitignored here so the bundled copy can never drift:

    cd app && cp ../schema/*.json assets/schema/

CI does exactly that before every build (see .github/workflows/app-release.yml).
Without this placeholder, `flutter build` fails on a clean clone until someone
happens to run the copy step — which is a confusing first-run experience for a
problem that a single tracked file prevents.

The same reasoning applies to `assets/fonts/.gitkeep`.
